@*
    OdsContactSelect — THE contact picker (Odyssey Design System · components/ContactSelect).

    The one control every field that links a record to a contact uses: the transaction counterparty,
    a file's "Issued by", a subscription's Company, the Analyze-file Merchant cell, the insured
    contact / insurer / beneficiary roles on a policy, the Contact kind of a contract party. It
    replaces the plain select-of-names each of those surfaces used to hand-roll, so every contact
    field searches, shows each candidate's ContactType glyph in its registry colour, and — where the
    caller allows it — creates a missing contact inline.

    It is NOT a new widget: it wraps OdsCombobox (typeahead, full keyboard, accessible name,
    keyboard-operable clear) in the standard label / help / error field chrome, the same way
    OdsCustodianSelect does for the account ↔ custodian link.

    Options are built from ACTIVE contacts only — an archived contact must not be linkable — while a
    value already pointing at an archived contact stays resolvable so the trigger keeps showing its
    name. A caller that already holds display options (the party dialogs, which pre-filter to the
    records still linkable in a role) passes Options instead of Contacts.

    Inline create: with AllowCreate (gate it on the caller's contacts.create claim), the popover
    offers ONE create row per contact type — a contact is a person or a company and the two are
    mutually exclusive — and OnCreate(name, kind) returns the created option so it is selected in the
    same gesture. A picker that can select a contact can add one: reaching a dead end because the
    contact doesn't exist yet is what sends people to another screen mid-task.

    Bare drops the label / help chrome for a control that sits in a table cell or inside a caller's
    own OdsFieldShell; it then names itself with AriaLabel (defaulting to Label).
*@

@if (Bare)
{
    @Control
}
else
{
    <div class="@FieldClass">
        <label class="odc-field-label" for="@_inputId">
            @Label
            @if (Required)
            {
                <span class="odc-field-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
            }
            else if (Optional)
            {
                <span class="odc-field-opt">Optional</span>
            }
        </label>

        @Control

        @* Both regions are ALWAYS mounted (empty when idle) so a later text change is announced — a
           region created together with its text usually isn't. At most one carries text at a time;
           the wrapper keeps them out of the field's flex gap so an empty region adds no space. *@
        <div class="odc-field-msgs">
            <div class="odc-field-help" id="@_statusId" role="status" aria-live="polite">@StatusMessage</div>
            <div class="odc-field-help error" id="@_alertId" role="alert">@AlertMessage</div>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    // Razor syntax, so it cannot live in the code-behind: the same control markup for both the bare
    // (table-cell) and the chromed form-field rendering, so the two can never drift apart.
    private RenderFragment Control =>
        @<OdsCombobox Value="@Value"
                      ValueChanged="OnValueChanged"
                      Options="_options"
                      Placeholder="@Placeholder"
                      Disabled="@PickerDisabled"
                      Loading="@Loading"
                      EmptyText="@EffectiveEmptyText"
                      InputId="@_inputId"
                      AriaLabel="@BareAriaLabel"
                      AriaDescribedBy="@(Bare ? null : _describedBy)"
                      Required="@Required"
                      Error="@HasError"
                      OnCreate="@(CanCreate ? HandleCreate : null)"
                      CreateLabel="@CreateLabel"
                      CreateKinds="@(CanCreate ? EffectiveCreateKinds : null)" />;
}
